// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`verifier handoff template snapshots > planner request renders the complete contract 1`] = `
"> ⚠️ **Template notice — not part of the message. Do not copy this notice into your handoff.**
> Recipient visibility: the \`verifier\` agent receives only the text inside your \`handoff --next-role="verifier"\` command. It cannot see anything you write in this agent session, or tool output. Put your complete deliverable in the handoff message.

Instructions (not part of the message): The verifier judges, from chatroom logs only, whether the user's last message was achieved. It runs no test the user did not ask for, and never builds, lints, or edits; list any user-requested tests under Requested test runs. Treat the claimed outcome as a claim, not as evidence: the verifier does not trust it and checks every requirement against the logs themselves. Request this review only when the task involved code changes, in any conversation mode. The verdict returns to \`planner\`.

Message template for \`planner\` (copy only the body sections below; do not copy this line, the notice, or the instructions after the body):

## Round
<1 or 2; for 2, cite the round-1 verdict message id>

## Mode
<chat | code | code:enhanced>

## User message id
<id of the user's last message: the origin message id of the user task, or from \`chatroom messages anchor\`>

## Context id
<id from \`chatroom context read\`, or \`none\` if no context was read for this task>

## Requested test runs
<the test commands the user explicitly asked for, one per line, or exactly \`None requested.\`>

## Claimed outcome
<requirement-by-requirement what you believe is complete>

## Evidence pointers
<builder handoff message ids, commits, PRs, and test results as quoted in those handoffs>

## Known gaps
<anything incomplete, or exactly \`None.\`>

Instructions after the body (not part of the message): run the normal handoff command to \`planner\` with the complete body above, then stop.

\`\`\`bash
chatroom handoff --chatroom-id="<chatroom-id>" --role="planner" --next-role="verifier" << 'CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END'
---MESSAGE---
[Your message here]
CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END
\`\`\`"
`;

